---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const effectiveDate = "September 16, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — SVGWire"
  description="SVGWire Terms of Service. Simple, clear terms governing the use of SVGWire's free client-side SVG conversion and sprite generation tools."
  canonical="https://svgwire.com/terms"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[860px] px-6 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-hairline pb-8">
      <h1 class="text-display-md text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="text-body-sm text-mute">Effective Date: {effectiveDate}</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Article Content -->
    <div class="space-y-10 text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
      <!-- 1. Acceptance of Terms -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          1. Acceptance of Terms
        </h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using the SVGWire website located at <a
            href="https://svgwire.com"
            class="text-ink underline hover:text-mute">https://svgwire.com</a
          > ("Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms").
          If you do not agree to these Terms, please do not use the Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Description of Service -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          2. Description of Service
        </h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire provides a free, browser-based web utility that transforms SVG
          (Scalable Vector Graphics) assets into frontend component code
          (including React, Vue 3, Svelte 5, React Native, and Tailwind CSS
          formats), compiles SVG sprite sheets, and converts folders of SVG
          files in batch.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Core SVG parsing, transformation, code generation, and archive
          compilation occur locally in your web browser. Standard network
          requests are made when your browser retrieves the Service's pages,
          stylesheets, fonts, and other static assets from third-party
          infrastructure providers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Acceptable Use -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          3. Acceptable Use
        </h2>
        <p>
          You agree to use the Service only for lawful purposes. You must not:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>
            Attempt to interfere with, disrupt, or compromise the integrity or
            security of the Service infrastructure.
          </li>
          <li>
            Use automated scripts, bots, or scraping tools to spam, overload, or
            maliciously attack the website.
          </li>
          <li>
            Use the Service to process or distribute content that is illegal,
            harmful, or infringes on the intellectual property rights of third
            parties.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. User Responsibility for Content -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          4. User Responsibility for Content
        </h2>
        <p>
          You are solely responsible for all SVG files, code, and content that
          you input into SVGWire or export using the Service. You represent and
          warrant that you possess all necessary rights, licenses, and
          permissions to use and convert the SVG assets you supply.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Intellectual Property -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          5. Intellectual Property
        </h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire and its original branding, website design, UI layout, logos,
          source code, and other original assets are owned by the operator of
          SVGWire and are protected by applicable copyright, trademark, and
          intellectual property laws.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          SVGWire claims no ownership interest or copyright in the SVG files you
          input or the converted component code output generated from your
          inputs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. Third-Party Assets and Trademarks -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          6. Third-Party Assets and Trademarks
        </h2>
        <p>
          Framework names and product trademarks referenced on SVGWire (such as
          React, Vue, Svelte, React Native, Tailwind CSS, Cloudflare, and Figma)
          belong to their respective trademark holders. Reference to these
          trademarks does not imply affiliation, sponsorship, or endorsement by
          those entity owners.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 7. Generated Code & Output -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          7. Generated Code & Output
        </h2>
        <p>
          Code generated by SVGWire is provided "as is". You are granted
          permission to copy, modify, integrate, and distribute the code
          generated from your inputs in both non-commercial and commercial
          software applications without attribution to SVGWire. SVGWire makes no
          claim of ownership over third-party assets or code structures embedded
          within your original SVG input.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 8. Service Availability -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          8. Service Availability
        </h2>
        <p>
          SVGWire is provided on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis. We reserve
          the right to modify, suspend, or discontinue any aspect of the Service
          at any time without prior notice or liability.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 9. Disclaimer of Warranties -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          9. Disclaimer of Warranties
        </h2>
        <p>
          TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE SERVICE IS
          PROVIDED WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, WHETHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
          INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
          FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, OR NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT
          WARRANT THAT THE GENERATED CODE WILL BE ERROR-FREE OR UNINTERRUPTED.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 10. Limitation of Liability -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          10. Limitation of Liability
        </h2>
        <p>
          IN NO EVENT SHALL SVGWIRE, ITS OPERATOR, OR CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE FOR
          ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES,
          OR LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, OR USE, ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH
          YOUR USE OR INABILITY TO USE THE SERVICE OR GENERATED CODE.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 11. Changes to Terms -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          11. Changes to Terms
        </h2>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to revise these Terms of Service at any time.
          Modified terms will become effective immediately upon posting to this
          page. Your continued use of the Service following any changes
          constitutes your acceptance of the updated Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- 12. Contact Information -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink mb-3 font-semibold">
          12. Contact Information
        </h2>
        <p>For questions regarding these Terms of Service, please contact:</p>
        <div
          class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-4 font-mono text-body-sm"
        >
          <p>
            Email: <a
              href="mailto:contact@svgwire.com"
              class="text-ink underline hover:text-mute">contact@svgwire.com</a
            >
          </p>
          <p>
            Website: <a
              href="https://svgwire.com"
              class="text-ink underline hover:text-mute">https://svgwire.com</a
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
